On Thursday, November 5, 2015 at 10:34:03 PM UTC-5, Ben Goodrich wrote:
> On Thursday, November 5, 2015 at 8:11:24 PM UTC-5, Andrew Gelman wrote:
> > No, Bayesian conventions predate Gibbs sampling.  I think the conventions come from various sources; different stories for different distributions.  One awkward example we’ve discussed on this list is that the exponential distribution is parameterized in terms of rate, and the Laplace double-exponential distribution is parameterized in terms of scale = 1/rate.
>
> What is Bayesian justification for using the rate parameterization for the exponential if not for the fact that it is conjugate with the rate-parameterized gamma distribution?
>

I'm pretty sure this just comes from the failure rate literature. Krzysztof

