In-Reply-To: <7a2nz9fhw6Q.uGaELnLiAQAJ@stan-users.groups.google.com>
References: <7a2nz9fhw6Q.uGaELnLiAQAJ@stan-users.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/stan-users/c/7a2nz9fhw6Q/m/n-jhD7LOAwAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

should be:

Omega <- multiply_lower_tri_self_transpose(L_Sigma);

The idea is just lkj_corr_cholesky samples a correlation matrix in cholesky form,
then we multiply L_sigma to L_Omega to get the cholesky form of the cov.
With L*L', where L is a chol. matrix we get the covariance matrix "back".
STAN has no cholesky form of multivariate studentt.

Hope it helps,
Andre

