On Tuesday, November 10, 2015 at 12:38:28 AM UTC-5, Emmanuel Charpentier wrote:
> Hmmm... if the Boost headers are already included, it could be possible to test for them and condition the inclusion of BH headers to the absence of Boost headers, no ?

I'm surprised that the header guards don't prevent the same file from being included twice. But I suspect part of the problem is that Boost in Sage still seems to be on 1.52, which is too old to use with Stan and probably has a lot of renamed files in the meantime.

> PS : How to formally report the problem (bug report) ?

We have GitHub repositories for reporting bugs, but I don't think this is a Stan bug. There have been reports from time to time of something like this happening on a Mac where an old Boost was installed to /usr/local/, but I think that was fixed for 2.8.

Ben

